\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cause Disease}{\fs24 
\par \tab Even a scratch fro
m a legendary monster can infect a character with a fatal malady. Each time a monster with this power makes a successful physical attack, secretly roll 1d100. If the result is equal to or less than the damage inflicted during the attack, the opponent cont
r
acts a disease. If the creature strikes an opponent multiple times in a single round, check for disease only once and use the total damage inflicted for the check. For example, if a creature strikes an opponent twice for 17 points of damage with the first
 hit and 21 points of damage with the second blow, the opponent contracts a disease on a roll of 38 or less.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Disease Effects
\par }{\fs24 \tab In addition to just feeling rotten\emdash and facing death if not cured\emdash the victim also suffers one to four of the following effects. Other effects are possible.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Ability Score Reduction:}{\fs24  One or all of the character\rquote s ability scores are reduced by one to five points.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Blindness:}{\fs24  The victim\rquote s vision blurs or the characters eyes swell shut. The character cannot cast spells or use missile weapons, and he suffers the standard penalties for blindness when moving or engaged in melee. A}{\i\fs24 
 cure blindness}{\fs24  spell has no effect,
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Chills:}{\fs24  The character shivers uncontrollably for 2d4 rounds. During this time, the character cannot move, attack, or cast spells. All saving throws and ability checks suffer a \endash 
4 penalty. The chills recur from time to time; roll again on the onset column to see how soon.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Delirium:}{\fs24  The victim\rquote s head spins with weird visions and confused thoughts. The character acts as though afflicted by a }{\i\fs24 confusion}{\fs24 
 spell. Once each turn, the victim can snap out of the delirium by rolling a 9 or less on 1d20. The victim\rquote s hit point adjustment (from Constitution/Health) applies as a bonus or penalty to the roll. Non\_
warrior characters with Constitution scores of 17 or higher can claim the warrior hit point adjustment for purposes of this roll.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Fever:}{\fs24  The character must rest in bed. If forced into action, the character\rquote s stamina is severely tested and he must roll a 9 or less on 1d20 each hour to stay conscious. The character\rquote 
s hit probability adjustment applies as a bonus or penalty to the roll. If the character has a Stamina statistic, use that score to determine the character\rquote s adjustment to the roll, otherwise use Strength. If the roll fails, the character suffers }
{\i\fs24 delirium}{\fs24  (as above) for 2d4 rounds and then falls into a stupor for 2d4 hours.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Paralyzation:}{\fs24  The character loses the use of one appendage or becomes totally immobile.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Slow healing:}{\fs24  The character cannot benefit from healing spells and heals naturally at 10% of the normal rate.
