\par }{\fs24 \tab A legendary monster can have minor, major, or extraordinary spell\_like abilities, as defined on page 49. The higher the creature\rquote s rank, the more often it can use its abilities.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Invulnerability (Physical)
\par }{\fs24 \tab Not every weapon can harm a legendary monster. This power can work in several different ways:
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Weapon Type:}{\fs24  The creature suffers no damage from a single type of weapon (bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing).
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Normal Weapon:}{\fs24  The creature suffers no damage from ordinary weapons and is harmed only by weapons made from a special material (silver, cold\_wrought iron, stone, wood, etc.).
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Nonmagical Weapon:}{\fs24 
 The creature can be harmed only by enchanted weapons. Lesser scions with this power usually can be harmed by +1 or better weapons. Scions and elders are harmed by +2 or better weapons, and great elders and paragons by +3 or better weapons.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Invulnerability (Elemental)
\par }{\fs24 The creature is immune to attacks based on one of the four elements: air, earth, fire, or water.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Invulnerability (Magical)}{\fs24 
\par The creature is immune to specific magical effects or classes of magical effects, such as charms, cold, holds, aging, energy drains, etc. Most legendary creatures have this power.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Enhanced Movement}{\fs24 
