\par Type: Animate, Imbue, Image
\par Range: Touch
\par Duration: 1 Week
\par Difficulty: 140
\par Final Difficulty: \endash 2
\par Preparation Time: None
\par Casting Time: 1 Round
\par Area of Effect: One object or group of objects weighing 50 pounds or less
\par Saving Throw: None
\par 
\par \tab This spell creates an animated messenger that moves at a speed of 12 to the location specified by the caster and delivers a spoken message 
of any length in a loud, clear voice. If sufficient duration remains after the herald delivers its message, the caster can instruct it to return with a written reply, which some person must attach to the herald. The herald can be programmed to perform spe
cific actions at certain times, subject to the spell duration.
\par \tab If more than one object is affected by the spell, they all must be given the same message and instructions. Only total destruction of the object, by a }{\i\fs24 disintegrate }{\fs24 or similar spell, can stop the herald from delivering its message.

\par \tab The material components are a seashell (common), a feather from a bird gifted with speech, a clock or other machine capable of independent operation, a powdered onyx worth at least 50 gp (rare), blood taken from a mim
ic while in an assumed form, and a leaf or seed from a tree animated by a treant and freely given (exotic).
