\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 All-around Attack: }{\fs24 A warrior with this skill is capable of launching a massive blow that can be extended into a whirlwind physical attack that damages every enemy within reach.
\par \tab An all\_around attack must be announced in a round\rquote s player determination step (see the }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Handbook}{\fs24 , Chapter 9). In the round\rquote 
s resolution step, the warrior makes a single attack roll against any adjacent opponent. If the attack hits, the opponent suffers normal damage from the blow. If the damage is sufficient to kill the oppo
nent, the hail of blows from the warrior automatically inflicts damage on every enemy within a 5\_foot radius, as decided by the character. Enemies who are larger than the original target, or whose Armor Classes are better than the original target\rquote 
s, are not harmed. Invisible opponents within the radius can be harmed if their effective Armor Classes (after the \endash 4 bonus for }{\i\fs24 invisibility}{\fs24 ) is not better than the original target\rquote s.
\par \tab An all\_around attack is a measure of a warrior\rquote s skill and can be made with any type of melee weapon that the warrior is proficient with. However, opponents that would normally be immune to the weapon used cannot be harmed in an all\_
around attack. If the initial attack misses, the all\_around attack fails. If the initial attack hits, the target suffers normal from the attack. If the damage inflicted fails to kill the original target, there is no radius effect.
\par \tab The warrior cannot move or take another action during the round when he attempts an all\_around attack. If the }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Option: Combat & Tactics }{\fs24 combat system is in use, an all\_
around attack cannot be used as an attack of opportunity or as part of a heroic fray.
\par \tab Beyond determining if the initial attack succeeds, the warrior\rquote s combat bonuses are not a factor in an all\_around attack. The damaged inflicted on creatures within the 5\_foot radius varies with the warrior\rquote s level as follows:
