\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Death Blow: }{\fs24 This skill allows warriors to strike deadly blows that can fell an opponent in a single stroke.
\par \tab A death blow must be announced in a round\rquote s player determination step. In the round\rquote 
s resolution step, the warrior makes a single attack roll against any adjacent opponent. If the attack hits, the opponent suffers normal damage from the blow and must save vs. death magic or be slain immediately. The opponent\rquote 
s defensive bonuses from protective devices (such as magical armor and }{\i\fs24 rings of protection}{\fs24 ) always apply to the saving throw. If the DM wishes, the optional saving throw modifiers from Table 36 or from Table 38 can be used as well.

\par \tab Opponents with more Hit Dice/levels than the warrior are immune to the effect. Creatures that would not normally be vulnerable to damage from the weapon the warrior is using in the attack also are immune.
\par \tab When a warrior attempts a death blow, that is the only attack a warrior can make during the round. Attacks of opportunity (see }{\i\fs24 Combat & Tactics}{\fs24 , Chapter 1) are allowed, however, and a warrior can combine a death blow with an all\_
around attack. Only the initial target of the all\_around attack is subject to the instant death effect, but this might allow the all\_around attack to succeed when it otherwise might not.
\par 
