\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Spell Talisman: }{\fs24 This skill allows a priest to cast one or more spells at the beginning of each day, making them available for instant use.
\par \tab When a priest with this skill is finished praying for spells, the character can attempt to cast the spell and direct its magical ener
gy into a special container or talisman. A talisman is a small object such as a jewel, crystal bead, or holy symbol blessed by the priest. A talisman must be worth at least 100 gp per spell level. 
\par \tab A successful skill roll is required to place a spell into
 a talisman. If the roll fails, the spell is wasted. The priest must have all necessary material components on hand and must meet all the usual requirements to cast a spell. If casting the spell has an effect on the priest, such as unnatural aging, the pr
iest suffers the effect even if the spell was not placed in the talisman.
\par \tab The total levels of spells a priest can have stored in talismans cannot exceed the priest\rquote s level. The highest level spell a priest can place in a talisman depends on the priest\rquote s level, as shown below:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx1800\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\adjustright {\b\fs24 Priest Level\tab Maximum Spell Level
\par }{\fs24 12\endash 14\tab 1st
\par 15\endash 17\tab 2nd
\par 18\endash 20\tab 3rd
\par 21\endash 23\tab 4th
\par 24\endash 26\tab 5th
\par 27\endash 29\tab 6th
\par 30+\tab 7th
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\adjustright {\fs24 \tab For example, Wulf, a 21st\_level priest, can have up to 21 levels of spells store
d, but no stored spell can be higher than 4th level. Wulf might choose to store two spells of 4th level, two 3rd, and seven 1st\_level spells.
\par \tab To release a spell from a talisman, the priest must be holding or carrying the item and have the opportunity to c
oncentrate briefly and utter a few words. Though the initiative modifier for releasing the spell is +2, the release cannot be disrupted (though a gagged or silenced priest could not release the spell). Once the spell is released, it functions as if cast n
ormally in all respects, destroying the talisman in the process.
\par \tab A spell can be stored in a talisman for a maximum of 24 hours. If not used in the allotted time, or if separated from the priest for more than one hour, the talisman crumbles into dust and th
e spell is lost. No being other than the priest who stored the spell can release the stored energy.
\par \tab A portion of the spell stored in a talisman lingers in the priest\rquote s memory. If the priest memorizes spells again before the 24 hours have expired, the char
acter cannot regain the spell stored in the talisman. The priest cannot transfer a spell from a talisman back into memory. If a talisman is destroyed, the spell is lost. A spell fades from the priest\rquote s memory when it is released or lost.
\par \tab Spells stored in 
talismans can be cast on worlds where the local magical factor would not allow the spell to be cast (see Chapter 2). A spell cannot be stored in talisman, however, unless the local conditions allow the spell to be cast. The initiative modifier for releasi
ng a spell from a talisman is never affected by the local magical factor.
