\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Improved Item Identification: }{\fs24 At 21st level, a bard can analyze magical items and determine something about their specific powers.
\par \tab For each hour a bard spends studying an item, the character has a 55% chance to determine a single power. The item\rquote s exact magical bonuses and number of charges are never revealed (see the 1st\_level wizard spell }{\i\fs24 identify}{\fs24 
). The bard need not handle the item or expend any materials, the character merely examines the item closely. 
\par 
