\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Fall/Jump:}{\b\fs24  }{\fs24 A rogue with this skill can safely break a fall if there is a vertical surface nearby to help slow the character\rquote s descent. A very accomplished rogue can fall or jump from amazing heights and not s
uffer the slightest injury.
\par \tab A successful skill check allows the rogue to make contact with a nearby surface and safely descend. The maximum distance from a vertical surface and the maximum distance for a safe fall depends of the rogue\rquote s level:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx2160\tx3600\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\adjustright {\b\fs24 \tab Surface\tab Distance
\par Rogue Level\tab Distance\tab Fallen
\par }{\fs24 11\endash 13\tab  1'\tab   30'
\par 14\endash 16\tab  2'\tab   60'
\par 17\endash 19\tab  3'\tab   90'
\par 20\endash 21\tab  5'\tab 120'
\par 22\endash 24\tab  7'\tab 150'
\par 25\endash 27\tab  9'\tab 180'
\par 28\endash 30\tab 11'\tab 210'
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab Rogues who simply s
tep off a precipice or fall while climbing are always within one foot of a vertical surface unless it has a negative slope (angled back under the place from which the rogue fell). Any surface that can provide a reasonable amount of friction when the rogue
 grabs it or places his hands or feet against it is sufficient (ropes, tree trunks, walls, etc.). Very smooth or slippery surfaces are useless (ice walls, greased poles, }{\i\fs24 walls of force}{\fs24 , etc.).
\par \tab If the fall is longer than the safe distance allowed for the rogue\rquote s level, subtract the safe distance from the total distance before determining damage from the fall. For example, a trap door opens under Jobare, a 20th\_
level thief, and dumps him into a shaft 10 feet square. No matter what happens, Jobare is within fi
ve feet of one wall, so he can attempt to break his fall. His skill roll succeeds, however, the shaft goes down 150 feet and then opens into a chamber 30 feet high and several hundred feet across. Jobare can break only the first 120 feet if his fall and s
uffers 6d6 points of damage for the final 60 feet. Even if he had been a 30th\_level thief, Jobare would have suffered 3d6 points of damage because there was no surface within reach to break the final 30 feet of the fall.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 Requirement: }{\fs24 Rogue 11+ 
\par }{\b\fs24 Relevant Ability: }{\fs24 Dexterity/Balance 
\par }{\b\fs24 Success: }{\fs24 11\tab }{\b\fs24 Cost: }{\fs24 1 (3)
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 Featherfoot: }{\fs24 Rogues with this skill can make their footsteps as light as a feather, moving silently and exerting very little pressure on the surface they are moving over.
\par \tab This skill is a function of the rogue\rquote 
s move silently ability, which is a requirement for using this skill. A rogue who makes a successful move silently roll can move a short distance over a surface fairly quickly and without exerting any appreciable weight on it, according to the table b
elow.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx1440\tx2880\tx4320\tx4680\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\adjustright {\b\fs24 Rogue Level\tab Surface\tab Distance*\tab Movement
\par }{\fs24 11\endash 13\tab Soft\tab   30'\tab \tab 12
\par 14\endash 16\tab Very Soft\tab   60'\tab \tab 15
\par 17+\tab Liquid\tab 120'\tab \tab 18
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\adjustright {\fs24 
\par * The rogue must stop and make contact with the surface after moving this far.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs24 Soft Surfaces: }{\fs24 Mud, snow, sand, or other surfaces where normal humans would leave clear tracks.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs24 Very Soft Surfaces: }{\fs24 Quicksand, fine dust, or other surfaces where normal humans would sink slowly.
\par 
\par }{\i\fs24 Liquid Surfaces: }{\fs24 Water or other surfaces where normal humans would sink immediately.
\par 
\par \tab A rogue using the featherfoot skill moves in complete silence and leaves no tracks on the ground. The character\rquote s weight doe not press down upon the surface at all. The character does not set off any alarm or trap triggered by weight and does 
not trigger a }{\i\fs24 squeaking floors }{\fs24 spell.
\par }{\b\fs24 Requirement: }{\fs24 Rogue 11+ 
